   "text": {
    "L1": "When we travel, we may need to add or subtract large numbers.",
    "L2": "First, line up ones under ones, tens under tens, and every other place value.",
    "L3": "In addition, add each column and carry 1 when a column reaches 10 or more.",
    "L4": "In subtraction, take the bottom digit from the top digit. Regroup when the top digit is too small.",
    "L5": "Watch 40,000 minus 12,368. The zeros cannot give directly, so break one ten-thousand.",
    "L6": "It becomes 3 ten-thousands, 9 thousands, 9 hundreds, 9 tens, and 10 ones.",
    "L7": "Now subtract each column to get 27,632, then check by adding 12,368 back.",
    "L8": "A zero that gives one away keeps 9. Only the ones place keeps 10, so not every zero becomes 10."
   },
